#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:230
msgid "Bluetooth call mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:232
msgid "When you start a video or voice call, your Bluetooth headset can switch to a special call mode that turns on the microphone — but the sound becomes mono and lower quality, like an old phone. This is off by default so music and movies stay in full quality even when an app asks for the microphone. Turn it on if you rely on the headset's microphone for calls."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:244
msgid "On — switch to call mode automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:245
msgid "Off — always keep stereo sound (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:255
msgid "Behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:262
msgid "Bluetooth audio buffer"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:264
msgid "Bluetooth needs a small audio reserve so the sound plays smoothly even when the wireless connection has tiny stutters. A bigger reserve hides hiccups but adds delay between picture and sound — keep the default unless your headset stutters or you need quicker audio."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:275
msgid "Small (low delay — needs a stable headset, ~11 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:278
msgid "Medium (~21 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:279
msgid "Standard (default, ~42 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:280
msgid "Large (steadiest, ~85 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:290
msgid "Buffer size"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:297
msgid "High-quality Bluetooth audio (SBC-XQ)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:299
msgid "Your Bluetooth devices already use the best sound mode they support. Force this on if a headset stubbornly chooses lower quality, or off if you have a very old device that breaks with the high-quality mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:308
msgid "Force on (high quality)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:309
msgid "Force off (maximum compatibility)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:319
msgid "SBC-XQ"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:328
msgid "Audio responsiveness"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:330
msgid "How fast the system reacts to sound changes. Faster reaction is great for music production but uses more CPU; slower reaction makes playback steadier on weaker machines. The default works well for video calls, music and games on most computers."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:340
msgid "Very fast (music production, ~5 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:341
msgid "Fast (low delay, ~11 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:343
msgid "Balanced (upstream PipeWire default, ~21 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:346
msgid "Steady (default, ~42 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:348
msgid "Most stable (older or busy machines, ~85 ms)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:360
msgid "Reaction speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:367
msgid "USB audio safety margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:369
msgid "A small extra reserve for USB headsets, microphones and external audio interfaces. Increase only if you hear tiny cuts or pops on a USB device when the computer is busy."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:384 src/ui/views/advanced.rs:409
msgid "Margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:391
msgid "Built-in audio safety margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:393
msgid "Same idea as the USB margin, but for the speakers and microphone built into your laptop or motherboard. Most people never need to change this — try it only if the internal speaker glitches when the computer is under load."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:416
msgid "Avoid the click at the start of sounds"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:418
msgid "Some laptops and motherboards put the speakers to sleep after a few seconds of silence to save power. When the next sound arrives — a notification, a video starting — you may hear a small click or miss the very first part of the audio. Turn this on to keep the speakers always ready. The extra battery use is tiny."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:430
msgid "Always keep the speakers ready (recommended on desktops)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:433
msgid "Let the speakers sleep when idle (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:443
msgid "Speaker sleep"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:452
msgid "Sound quality range"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:454
msgid "All audio runs at studio quality (48 kHz) by default. Hi-res music players and high-end USB DACs can play higher quality if you allow it here, but every change between qualities causes a brief audio reload. Keep the default unless you actually own hi-res equipment."
msgstr ""

